# Constituents of the self-host differential family whose SURFACE does not exist
# yet, read by scripts/selfhost-diffall.sh. One script basename per line.
#
# An entry here excuses exit 2 (could-not-decide) and NOTHING else: a listed
# script that reports a real divergence still fails the run. This is not a
# mute button, it is a record of what has not been built.
#
# Delete an entry the moment its surface lands — the differential goes green on
# its own, and leaving it listed would keep tolerating a future exit 2.

# The self-hosted `bit` has no `fmt` subcommand at all (#1542). difffmt.sh is
# written to be the gate for porting it, not a report of it.
selfhost-difffmt.sh
